 "note": "Two arms curl out of a rotor core (half-turn symmetry). The rotor joins the arm tips (north / south, r1) or the inner pockets (west / east, r2), so the shortest road swaps between the arms. Wide 90 curves, flex S-bridges into the pockets, a long bottom / top lane to the enemy arm tip. [KEEP edit 2026-11-11: belts on the two round (Wide 90) bridges, flowing from each home's arm toward the centre.]",
 "geometricSymmetry": true,
